Hide pathhide-matched files from /proc/<pid>/maps, smaps, smaps_rollup,
numa_maps and /proc/<pid>/fd (readdir, lookup, readlink and fdinfo).

Generated hunk by hunk against the real tree the fleet pins for this kernel
version:

    OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_common_oneplus_sm8450 @ oneplus/sm8450_b_16.0_oneplus_10_pro

and dry-run at fuzz 0 against every distinct fs/proc variant the manifests
resolve to. A hunk that only lands "with fuzz" can silently guard the wrong
function, so treat a fuzz report from `patch` as a failure and regenerate.

Version notes:
  * proc_readfd_count()/proc_fd_getattr() do not exist here, so there is no
    kernel-supplied fd count for stat(/proc/<pid>/fd).st_size to leak -- that
    fix is N/A on this version, not skipped.
  * tid_fd_mode() takes a files_struct reference and uses fcheck_files(); the
    file carries no reference, so the guard just drops it on the floor.
  * show_map()/show_smap() are wrapped rather than guarded inline: on this tree
    they open with get_pad_vma()/get_data_vma(), which hand back kzalloc'd
    copies that only show_map_pad_vma() frees. An early return placed after
    those declarations would leak two struct vm_area_struct per hidden padded
    mapping, once per read of /proc/<pid>/maps.
  * smaps_rollup iterates `for (vma = priv->mm->mmap; vma;)` with the advance
    at the bottom of the body, so the guard suppresses the accumulation rather
    than using `continue`, which would spin forever.
